   <span class=\"tag\">Hacker News</span>\n   328→                    </div>\n   329→                </div>\n   330→\n   331→                <div class=\"item\">\n   332→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49283063\" target=\"_blank\">Bullet</a></div>\n   333→                    <div class=\"item-description\">YC S26 coding agent launched on Hacker News, founded by Adi and Alex, described as a faster coding agent that addresses slow performance of existing agents like Claude Code.</div>\n   334→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   335→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-08-15</span>\n   336→                        <span class=\"tag source-tag\">YC S26</span>\n   337→                        <span class=\"tag\">code agent</span>\n   338→                        <span class=\"tag\">Hacker News</span>\n   339→                    </div>\n   340→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Faster coding agent addressing Claude Code slowness\"</div>\n   341→                </div>\n   342→\n   343→                <div class=\"item\">\n   344→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/ito-ai-code-review-that-runs-code\" target=\"_blank\">Ito</a></div>\n   345→                    <div class=\"item-description\">AI code review tool that runs your application before reviewing code, using ephemeral environments to validate impacted flows and return runtime evidence for pull requests.</div>\n   346→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   347→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-08-13</span>\n   348→                        <span class=\"tag source-tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   349→                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow-specific</span>\n   350→                    </div>\n   351→                    <div class=\"quote\">#4 of the Week for August 13th, 2026</div>\n   352→                </div>\n   353→            </section>\n   354→\n   355→            <!-- Whitelist Updates Column (35%) -->\n   356→            <section class=\"column\" id=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   357→                <div class=\"section-header\">\n   358→                    Product Updates <span class=\"count\">(11)</span>\n   359→                </div>\n   360→\n   361→                <div class=\"item\">\n   362→                    <div class=\"update-type\">Feature</div>\n   363→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12138966-release-notes\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code: Memory in Claude Cowork</a></div>\n   364→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Memory now works across chat and Cowork in the cloud, with editable topics and a new sensitive topics setting that keeps items like health or beliefs out of memory unless enabled.</div>\n   365→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   366→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-08-25</span>\n   367→                        <a href=\"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12138966-release-notes\" target=\"_blank\">Release Notes →</a>\n   368→                    </div>\n   369→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Memory enabled under Settings > Capabilities\"</div>\n   370→                </div>\n   371→\n   372→                <div class=\"item\">\n   373→                    <div class=\"update-type\">Release</div>\n   374→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://aider.chat/HISTORY.html\" target=\"_blank\">Aider: Claude 4.5/4.6, Gemini 2.5, DeepSeek Reasoner</a></div>\n   375→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Added support for Claude 4.5/4.6 models, expanded Gemini model support with 2.5 Flash/Lite and 3 preview, added DeepSeek Reasoner model, and improved exception handling.</div>\n   376→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   377→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-08-25</span>\n   378→                        <a href=\"https://aider.chat/HISTORY.html\" target=\"_blank\">History →</a>\n   379→                    </div>\n   380→                    <div class=\"quote\">Aider wrote 62% of the code in this release</div>\n   381→                </div>\n   382→\n   383→                <div class=\"item\">\n   384→                    <div class=\"update-type\">Release</div>\n   385→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Codex CLI 0.149.1: Agent Dashboard</a></div>\n   386→                    <div class=\"item-description\">New release adds interactive agents dashboard, working directory commands, queue for sessions, and expanded Vim editing.</div>\n   387→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   388→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-08-24</span>\n   389→                        <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Changelog →</a>\n   390→                    </div>\n   391→                </div>\n   392→\n   393→                <div class=\"item\">\n   394→                    <div class=\"update-type\">Announcement</div>\n   395→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Codex CLI: MCP Server Command Deprecated</a></div>\n   396→                    <div class=\"item-description\">The `codex mcp-server` command is now deprecated. Users should use the Codex app server instead, or the Codex plugin for Claude Code.</div>\n   397→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   398→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-08-24</span>\n   399→                        <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Changelog →</a>\n   400→                    </div>\n   401→                </div>\n   402→\n   403→                <div class=\"item\">\n   404→                    <div class=\"update-type\">Release</div>\n   405→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-08-21-the-new-github-copilot-experience-in-slack/\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot: Slack and Teams Integration</a></div>\n   406→                    <div class=\"item-description\">GitHub Copilot now brings shared agentic work to Slack and Microsoft Teams, allowing teams to collaborate with AI directly in their communication platforms.</div>\n   407→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   408→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-08-21</span>\n   409→                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-08-21-the-new-github-copilot-experience-in-slack/\" target=\"_blank\">Details →</a>\n   410→                    </div>\n   411→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Try building with @github Copilot directly in Slack or Teams\"</div>\n   412→                </div>\n   413→\n   414→                <div class=\"item\">\n   415→                    <div class=\"update-type\">Feature</div>\n   416→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Cursor: Cloud Agents and Harness Improvements</a></div>\n   417→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Continued improvements to cloud agents and the Cursor harness system. Agents can now monitor PRs, watch Slack threads, and run scheduled tasks with subscriptions.</div>\n   418→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   419→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-08-19</span>\n   420→                        <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Changelog →</a>\n   421→                    </div>\n   422→                </div>\n   423→\n   424→                <div class=\"item\">\n   425→                    <div class=\"update-type\">Release</div>\n   426→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog/origin-code-hosting\" target=\"_blank\">Cursor: Origin Code Hosting Platform</a></div>\n   427→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Cursor launched Origin, a new code hosting platform and GitHub alternative. Features include repos, pull requests, issues, code review, and integrations with Vercel, Depot, and Buildkite.</div>\n   428→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   429→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-08-17</span>\n   430→                        <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog/origin-code-hosting\" target=\"_blank\">Learn More →</a>\n   431→                    </div>\n   432→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Origin - Cursor's code hosting platform is now live!\"</div>\n   433→                </div>\n   434→\n   435→                <div class=\"item\">\n   436→                    <div class=\"update-type\">Feature</div>\n   437→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Cursor: Cloud Agents Start 3x Faster</a></div>\n   438→                    <div class=\"item-description\">New Builds system provides pre-configured environments that agents boot into, delivering 10x faster environment boot and 3x faster time to first token.</div>\n   439→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   440→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-08-13</span>\n   441→                        <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Changelog →</a>\n   442→                    </div>\n   443→                </div>\n   444→\n   445→                <div class=\"item\">\n   446→                    <div class=\"update-type\">Release</div>\n   447→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot: Grok 4.6 and Gemini 3.7 Flash</a></div>\n   448→                    <div class=\"item-description\">New AI models Grok 4.6 and Gemini 3.7 Flash are now available in GitHub Copilot, providing developers with more model choices for AI-assisted coding.</div>\n   449→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   450→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-08-14</span>\n   451→                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\">Changelog →</a>\n   452→                    </div>\n   453→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Gemini-3.7-flash is surprisingly pleasant to use. I prefer it.\"</div>\n   454→                </div>\n   455→\n   456→                <div class=\"item\">\n   457→                    <div class=\"update-type\">Feature</div>\n   458→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12138966-release-notes\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code: Security Scanning for Enterprise</a></div>\n   459→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Enterprise plans received beta access to skill and plugin security scanning, which automatically checks third-party skills and plugins for malicious content.</div>\n   460→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   461→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-08-06</span>\n   462→                        <a href=\"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12138966-release-notes\" target=\"_blank\">Release Notes →</a>\n   463→                    </div>\n   464→                </div>\n   465→\n   466→                <div class=\"item\">\n   467→                    <div class=\"update-type\">Feature</div>\n   468→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Cursor: Google Workspace Plugins</a></div>\n   469→                    <div class=\"item-description\">New integration with Google Workspace including Gmail for email management, Google Drive for file access and organization, and Google Calendar for scheduling.</div>\n   470→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   471→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-08-03</span>\n   472→                        <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Changelog →</a>\n   473→                    </div>\n   474→                </div>\n   475→            </section>\n   476→\n   477→            <!-- Technical Insights Column (25%) -->\n   478→            <section class=\"column\" id=\"technical-insights\">\n   479→                <div class=\"section-header\">\n   480→                    Technical Insights <span class=\"count\">(8)</span>\n   481→                </div>\n   482→\n   483→                <div class=\"item\">\n   484→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48861923\" target=\"_blank\">Why write code in 2026</a></div>\n   485→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Hacker News discussion on the role of manual coding in 2026. Covers debates on whether developers should still write code manually or rely entirely on AI agents.</div>\n   486→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   487→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-08-25</span>\n   488→                        <span class=\"source\">softwaredoug | HN</span>\n   489→                    </div>\n   490→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   491→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI coding</span>\n   492→                        <span class=\"tag\">human vs AI</span>\n   493→                        <span class=\"tag\">LLM limitations</span>\n   494→                    </div>\n   495→                </div>\n   496→\n   497→                <div class=\"item\">\n   498→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.21107\" target=\"_blank\">LLMs at Software Engineering and Security Intersection</a></div>\n   499→                    <div class=\"item-description\">August 24, 2026 arXiv paper presenting an evidence-centered structured survey and research agenda on LLMs in software engineering and security.</div>\n   500→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   501→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-08-24</span>\n   502→                        <span class=\"source\">ArXiv Research</span>\n   503→                    </div>\n   504→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   505→                        <span class=\"tag\">LLM security</span>\n   506→                        <span class=\"tag\">survey</span>\n   507→                        <span class=\"tag\">research</span>\n   508→                    </div>\n   509→                </div>\n   510→\n   511→                <div class=\"item\">\n   512→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.20844\" target=\"_blank\">TRACE: Agentic Catalog Enrichment</a></div>\n   513→                    <div class=\"item-description\">August 24, 2026 arXiv paper on agentic systems for catalog enrichment using multi-source evidence grounding.</div>\n   514→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   515→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-08-24</span>\n   516→                        <span class=\"source\">ArXiv Research</span>\n   517→                    </div>\n   518→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   519→                        <span class=\"tag\">agentic systems</span>\n   520→                        <span class=\"tag\">multi-source AI</span>\n   521→                    </div>\n   522→                </div>\n   523→\n   524→                <div class=\"item\">\n   525→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.20786\" target=\"_blank\">Multi-Agent Document Authoring</a></div>\n   526→                    <div class=\"item-description\">August 24, 2026 arXiv paper on multi-agent document authoring with asymmetric structural conditioning.</div>\n   527→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   528→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-08-24</span>\n   529→                        <span class=\"source\">ArXiv Research</span>\n   530→                    </div>\n   531→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   532→                        <span class=\"tag\">multi-agent systems</span>\n   533→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI collaboration</span>\n   534→                    </div>\n   535→                </div>\n   536→\n   537→                <div class=\"item\">\n   538→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46923543\" target=\"_blank\">Coding agents have replaced every framework I used</a></div>\n   539→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Hacker News discussion on replacing frameworks with AI-generated code. Key insights on AWS SRE agents, 'vibe coding' concerns, and framework mental models.</div>\n   540→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   541→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-08-24</span>\n   542→                        <span class=\"source\">alainrk | HN</span>\n   543→                    </div>\n   544→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   545→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI agents</span>\n   546→                        <span class=\"tag\">frameworks</span>\n   547→                        <span class=\"tag\">maintainability</span>\n   548→                    </div>\n   549→                </div>\n   550→\n   551→                <div class=\"item\">\n   552→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49378768\" target=\"_blank\">Show HN: Huzzah – Novel Approach to AI Coding</a></div>\n   553→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Hacker News discussion highlighting a novel approach to AI coding with selective assistance patterns.</div>\n   554→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   555→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-08-21</span>\n   556→                        <span class=\"source\">Hacker News</span>\n   557→                    </div>\n   558→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   559→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI coding tools</span>\n   560→                        <span class=\"tag\">productivity</span>\n   561→                    </div>\n   562→                </div>\n   563→\n   564→                <div class=\"item\">\n   565→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49161518\" target=\"_blank\">LLMs Reward Expertise</a></div>\n   566→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Hacker News discussion about CLI coding tools including Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Pi and their different capabilities.</div>\n   567→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   568→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-08-19</span>\n   569→                        <span class=\"source\">Hacker News</span>\n   570→                    </div>\n   571→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   572→                        <span class=\"tag\">CLI tools</span>\n   573→                        <span class=\"tag\">Claude Code</span>\n   574→                        <span class=\"tag\">Codex</span>\n   575→                    </div>\n   576→                </div>\n   577→\n   578→                <div class=\"item\">\n   579→                    <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://blog.jetbrains.com/research/2026/08/ai-coding-agent-adoption-2026/\" target=\"_blank\">AI Coding Agents: Adoption Trends</a></div>\n   580→                    <div class=\"item-description\">JetBrains Developer Ecosystem Survey 2026 findings on AI coding agent adoption. Claude Code leads at 39% adoption, GitHub Copilot declined to 21%.</div>\n   581→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   582→                        <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-08-18</span>\n   583→                        <span class=\"source\">JetBrains Blog</span>\n   584→                    </div>\n   585→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   586→                        <span class=\"tag\">adoption statistics</span>\n   587→                        <span class=\"tag\">Claude Code</span>\n   588→                        <span class=\"tag\">survey</span>\n   589→                    </div>\n   590→                </div>\n   591→            </section>\n   592→        </main>\n   593→\n   594→        <footer>\n   595→            <a href=\"#\">Report generated by Agent Code Daily</a> - Powered by <a href=\"#\">Claude Agent SDK</a> | Generated: 2026-08-25 23:04:59 |\n   596→            <a href=\"#new-products\">New Products</a> |\n   597→            <a href=\"#whitelist-updates\">Updates</a> |\n   598→            <a href=\"#technical-insights\">Insights</a>\n   599→        </footer>\n   600→    </div>\n   601→</body>\n   602→</html>"
